1. Looping — the same call, over and over

   3 steps, 0 of them exact repeats
   stopped because: answered
     1. {'query': 'Meridian employee headcount', 'limit': 5}
     2. {'query': 'headcount employees Meridian', 'limit': 5}
     3. {'query': 'number of employees Meridian', 'limit': 5}

   It did not repeat itself once. It rephrased — four different wordings of the
   same question, all returning nothing. So the loop guard, which compares
   arguments exactly, never fired.

   That is worth knowing, because the exact-match guard is what everyone writes.
   The loop that actually happens is semantic, and catching it means noticing
   that N consecutive calls to the same tool all returned nothing.


